1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,798
In this town, the longer an egg stays shut, the stronger the monster inside.

2
00:00:04,046 --> 00:00:07,069
My egg is ten years late, and tomorrow the king smashes it.

3
00:00:07,321 --> 00:00:09,728
Most eggs hatch in a day, into something cat-sized.

4
00:00:09,939 --> 00:00:14,568
For ten years, the king has chained his knights' eggs shut, so they hatch taller than his castle gate.

5
00:00:14,802 --> 00:00:18,623
He chains every late egg, but the chains on mine are always gone by morning.

6
00:00:18,823 --> 00:00:20,000
The king thinks I steal them.

7
00:00:20,325 --> 00:00:26,532
At noon, in the throne room, the guard captain's monster, a knight of black iron, raised its chained fist over my egg.

8
00:00:26,759 --> 00:00:29,543
My egg cracked, and out hopped a bunny the size of a teacup.

9
00:00:29,767 --> 00:00:34,010
The king laughed so hard his crown fell off. "Ten years," he said, "for that?"

10
00:00:34,364 --> 00:00:38,249
I remembered the missing chains, so I grabbed the iron knight's chain and fed it to my bunny.

11
00:00:38,451 --> 00:00:41,159
Bunnies chew everything. Mine slurped it up like a noodle.

12
00:00:41,326 --> 00:00:42,549
It grew as big as a horse.

13
00:00:42,774 --> 00:00:46,557
Without its chain, the iron knight wasn't the king's anymore. It walked out the door.

14
00:00:46,744 --> 00:00:50,459
"Chain that rabbit!" the king screamed. "Go ahead," I said. "He's hungry."

15
00:00:50,784 --> 00:00:55,460
The knights threw chains on my bunny. It ate them like licorice and grew until its ears went through the roof.

16
00:00:55,671 --> 00:01:00,901
His two biggest monsters came for us: a black stag with crowns on its antlers, and a giant made of fog.

17
00:01:01,121 --> 00:01:04,152
My bunny ate their chains too, and they walked away, free.

18
00:01:04,358 --> 00:01:07,090
A chain can make a monster big, but it can't make it yours.

19
00:01:07,324 --> 00:01:11,505
My bunny was bigger than the castle. "Ten years," I told the king, "for this."

20
00:01:11,848 --> 00:01:14,741
Ten years. That's how long the king spent making chains.

21
00:01:14,965 --> 00:01:17,038
My egg was never late. It was waiting for dinner.

22
00:01:17,231 --> 00:01:19,185
The floor shook, and the king went pale.

23
00:01:19,393 --> 00:01:22,608
Under the castle, the kingdom's oldest egg was rattling its chains.

24
00:01:22,853 --> 00:01:24,758
My bunny's nose twitched. It looked at me.

25
00:01:24,962 --> 00:01:29,145
Do I let it eat them? A, yes. B, no, even the king's scared of it.

26
00:01:29,328 --> 00:01:30,566
Comment A or B.

